* Constant On-Time Lab -- generic buck power-stage blocks
* Educational PSpice-oriented text library. No vendor models are used.
* Positive phase current flows VIN/SW -> inductor -> OUT.
* CAD-PSPICE-UG: Cadence PSpice A/D User Guide, Analog Behavioral Modeling.

.MODEL SW_COTLAB VSWITCH (RON=1u ROFF=1G VON=3 VOFF=1)
.MODEL D_BODY_COTLAB D (IS=10n N=1.05 RS=10m TT=5n CJO=20p)
.MODEL D_FAST_COTLAB D (IS=1n N=1 RS=1m TT=1n CJO=2p)

* BUCK_PHASE VIN OUT GHS GLS SW IMON
* IMON uses 1 V/A by default. SW is intentionally exposed for inspection.
* Channel resistance is modeled explicitly in series with each ideal switch.
* Body diodes establish a path during dead time and for reverse current.
.SUBCKT BUCK_PHASE VIN OUT GHS GLS SW IMON PARAMS:
+ LPH=1u DCR=5m RHS=10m RLS=5m IMONGAIN=1
RHSER VIN NHS {RHS}
SHS NHS SW GHS 0 SW_COTLAB
RLSER SW NLS {RLS}
SLS NLS 0 GLS 0 SW_COTLAB
DHS SW VIN D_BODY_COTLAB
DLS 0 SW D_BODY_COTLAB
LPHASE SW NL {LPH}
RDCR NL NSENSE {DCR}
VILSENSE NSENSE OUT 0
EIMON IMON 0 VALUE={I(VILSENSE)*IMONGAIN}
RIMON IMON 0 1G
.ENDS BUCK_PHASE

* Idealized switched phase. It retains finite switch on/off resistance so the
* nodal problem remains solvable; set RHS/RLS/DCR to zero only with care.
.SUBCKT BUCK_PHASE_IDEAL VIN OUT GHS GLS SW IMON PARAMS:
+ LPH=1u IMONGAIN=1
SHS VIN SW GHS 0 SW_COTLAB
SLS SW 0 GLS 0 SW_COTLAB
DHS SW VIN D_FAST_COTLAB
DLS 0 SW D_FAST_COTLAB
LPHASE SW NSENSE {LPH}
VILSENSE NSENSE OUT 0
EIMON IMON 0 VALUE={I(VILSENSE)*IMONGAIN}
RIMON IMON 0 1G
.ENDS BUCK_PHASE_IDEAL

* Averaged CCM phase. DUTY is a dimensionless voltage (0 V -> 0, 1 V -> 1).
* EAVG produces d*VIN at SW. This is not a switching waveform and is not valid
* for switching ripple, DCM, pulse skipping, or sampled-data effects.
.SUBCKT BUCK_AVERAGED VIN DUTY OUT IMON PARAMS:
+ LPH=1u DCR=5m IMONGAIN=1
EAVG SW 0 VALUE={LIMIT(V(DUTY),0,1)*V(VIN)}
LPHASE SW NL {LPH}
RDCR NL NSENSE {DCR}
VILSENSE NSENSE OUT 0
EIMON IMON 0 VALUE={I(VILSENSE)*IMONGAIN}
RIMON IMON 0 1G
.ENDS BUCK_AVERAGED

* Complementary gate driver with delayed rising edges and diode-bypassed
* falling edges. DEAD ~= 0.693*RDEAD*CDEAD at the 50% threshold.
* This is a timing abstraction, not a MOSFET gate-charge model.
.SUBCKT COMPLEMENTARY_DRIVER PWM GHS GLS PARAMS:
+ VLOGIC=5 DEAD=20n CDEAD=10p RDRIVE=1G
EHRAW HRAW 0 VALUE={LIMIT(V(PWM),0,VLOGIC)}
ELRAW LRAW 0 VALUE={VLOGIC-LIMIT(V(PWM),0,VLOGIC)}
RH HRAW HDELAY {IF(DEAD>0,DEAD/(0.693*CDEAD),1m)}
CH HDELAY 0 {CDEAD} IC=0
DH HDELAY HRAW D_FAST_COTLAB
RL LRAW LDELAY {IF(DEAD>0,DEAD/(0.693*CDEAD),1m)}
CL LDELAY 0 {CDEAD} IC={VLOGIC}
DL LDELAY LRAW D_FAST_COTLAB
EHOUT GHS 0 VALUE={IF(V(HDELAY)>VLOGIC/2,VLOGIC,0)}
ELOUT GLS 0 VALUE={IF(V(LDELAY)>VLOGIC/2,VLOGIC,0)}
RGH GHS 0 {RDRIVE}
RGL GLS 0 {RDRIVE}
.ENDS COMPLEMENTARY_DRIVER

* Enable-aware wrapper for phase shedding. ENABLE=0 forces both gate commands
* low; it must not be replaced by PWM=0, because PWM=0 commands synchronous
* low-side conduction. VENHIGH is the asserted enable-signal voltage.
* COMPLEMENTARY_DRIVER_ENABLE PWM ENABLE GHS GLS
.SUBCKT COMPLEMENTARY_DRIVER_ENABLE PWM ENABLE GHS GLS PARAMS:
+ VLOGIC=5 VENHIGH=1 DEAD=20n CDEAD=10p RDRIVE=1G
XCORE PWM GHRAW GLRAW COMPLEMENTARY_DRIVER PARAMS:
+ VLOGIC={VLOGIC} DEAD={DEAD} CDEAD={CDEAD} RDRIVE={RDRIVE}
EENABLE EN01 0 VALUE={LIMIT(V(ENABLE)/VENHIGH,0,1)}
EGHEN GHS 0 VALUE={V(GHRAW)*V(EN01)}
EGLEN GLS 0 VALUE={V(GLRAW)*V(EN01)}
RGHEN GHS 0 1G
RGLEN GLS 0 1G
.ENDS COMPLEMENTARY_DRIVER_ENABLE
